# SaathVerse has two env files. Copy each example next to it:
#   backend/.env.example   -> backend/.env
#   frontend/.env.example  -> frontend/.env.local
# scripts/setup.sh does this for you and generates a JWT secret.
#
# Backend (server side only)
#   JWT_SECRET          at least 32 random characters (required in production)
#   WEB_ORIGIN          where the frontend runs, for CORS and sockets
#   DATABASE_PATH       SQLite file, default ./data/saathverse.db
#   ADMIN_INVITE_CODE   code needed to create an admin account (dev default SAATH-ADMIN-2026)
#   DEMO_LOGIN          set to off to hide the one click demo accounts
#   SEED_DEMO           set to off to start with an empty database
#
# Frontend
#   API_ORIGIN              server side only: where the backend runs
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL  public: Socket.IO endpoint
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL    public: canonical site address
